{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the LAN address keys head (rate-limit keys behind a local proxy). The head is cd9497ab433f41f86cfd164915af41299cd0ec35 (tree fab1178c), for request 7ee9a63b (child of e6a5cd22, item 3), under builder promise a2d7366f. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nI read the implementation note 9e401d1c first. Then I read the request, the parent request and every change from Main eb827cc2.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- Base and delta. The head descends from Main eb827cc2 through 4 commits. They change exactly the 13 paths named by the 13 artifacts, one artifact per path, and all 13 are listed `current`. The worktree was clean at the head.\n- Checkpoints. de09f048 holds the source change. ea35a4d3 changes only apps/room/page/assets.ts. From ea35a4d3 to the head, only the note and its manifest are added.\n- First gate, at de09f048:\n  - It exited 1, with the source unchanged before and after.\n  - Its only failure is the Page bundle equality case in apps/room/page/test/assets.test.ts. Native was not reached.\n  - It remains failed.\n- Repair. The retained output of the pure `pageAssets()` generator at de09f048 has SHA-256 b112fb58…. apps/room/page/assets.ts at ea35a4d3 and at the head has the same SHA-256, and ea35a4d3 changes no other file. The Page bundle includes the Bytes barrel, so adding the export made this regeneration necessary.\n- Final gate, at ea35a4d3:\n  - It is a full ordinary gate, not a limited follow-up.\n  - It exited 0, with the source unchanged before and after. The output ends \"gate passed\", and all four phases passed:\n    - node 76;\n    - counting 55;\n    - plain 2900 passed and 1 skipped;\n    - Native 823 passed and 2 skipped.\n  - The focused Page asset run at ea35a4d3 also exited 0.\n- Owning runs at de09f048. Node, the four compilers and the focused Native run (limits.test.ts and hosted.scope.test.ts) each exited 0 with the source unchanged.\n- Controls, both through scripts/control.mjs at de09f048, both exit 0 (\"distinguishes\"):\n  - Classifier control: `first = 0` makes 2 of the 4 address cases fail by assertion, including the expected one ('local range ends …'). For example, fe80::1 gives `v6:fe80:0:0:0`.\n  - Bearer control: `key = raw` makes 5 of the 6 bearer cases fail, including the link-local alias case.\n- Evidence:\n  - The committed manifest has SHA-256 7fdcf111…. All 162 entries match their recorded size and hash, and no entry is writable.\n  - SHA256SUMS has 161 lines, all OK.\n  - The report tail's SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 1e4d9e72…, and all its 34 lines are OK. Its three document checks exited 0, its source proof names the head, and nothing in it is writable.\n  - Each output digest in the note's table matches its retained output.\n- Documents:\n  - check-doc-links on an export of the head: 728 links, 0 broken.\n  - check-notes eb827cc2..cd9497ab: 0 warnings.\n  - check-commit-messages: 4 checked, 0 flagged.\n  - `git diff --check`: clean.\n\nI reran no suite.\n\n## Architecture\n\n- `addressKey` moves to packages/bytes/src/address.ts. Except for the comment and two new branches, its body is the same as the version removed from limits.ts.\n- Scope re-exports it, so its public API and its three callers are unchanged: the join window, serving-admission and serving-limits. MCP imports it from Bytes and gains no new dependency.\n- The new branches use the full canonical 128 bits for fe80::/10 (`v6l:`) and fc00::/7 (`v6u:`). Other IPv6 keeps its /64 key, and IPv4 and IPv4-mapped IPv6 keep `v4:`.\n- The tests cover:\n  - each range's end points (fe80, febf, fc00, fdff);\n  - the adjacent ranges that stay /64 (fe7f, fec0, fbff, fe00);\n  - compression, padding, case and zones;\n  - the mapped forms;\n  - nine malformed inputs.\n- `BearerFailures.check` still checks the raw 64-character and 64-byte bounds first. Only then does it key by `addressKey(address) ?? \"\"`.\n- The route-level join test (T39) and the hosted H4 bearer test now use link-local addresses. Each shows a limited client, a second client on the same /64 that is served, and an expanded, zoned spelling of the first client that is limited. The pure JoinLimits test shows that two global addresses in one /64 still share a window. IPv4 behaviour is unchanged, and the pure tests still cover it.\n- The entry-points document gains the key table and states the new MCP bounds in all three bearer rows. The source seals cover the new owner and the barrel, and they are updated for limits.ts and hosted.ts. No native pin, setting, Site policy or proxy configuration changes.\n\n## Security\n\n- Trusted transport boundary. The key still comes only from `CF-Connecting-IP`, and the head changes no forwarding or origin policy. On Cloudflare Workers the platform sets that header, and a public client address is never link-local or unique-local. So hosted deployments see no change except stricter alias matching.\n- Aliases. Equivalent spellings and zones now share one window everywhere. Before, the MCP counter keyed by the raw string, so `fe80::1` and `FE80:0:…:1%en0` were separate windows. This change is stricter.\n- Invalid addresses. A missing address and a malformed address now share one MCP failure window, so neither bypasses the limit. Before, each malformed string had its own window. A malformed value can reach this code only where a client controls the header (direct celld, as validation V4.7 showed). A client that controls the header can already claim any valid address, so this adds no exposure.\n- Callback ordering. The bound check comes before canonicalization, and the window check comes before `authenticate`. The tests' `expect.fail` callbacks show that a limited key never reaches bearer authentication.\n\nOne point, not blocking. Full keys for local addresses change how fast a single LAN host can use up the bounded tables:\n- ServingLimits holds 8192 windows. When it is full it refuses every new identity, including a new verified key, and it never evicts an active window. Creation windows last one hour; read windows last one minute.\n- BearerFailures holds 4096 keys. When full, it refuses new failing addresses, but it still serves a valid bearer.\n\nBefore this head, all clients on one local /64 shared one key. Now a host that rotates its link-local or unique-local addresses gets a new key for each address, so it can fill the serving table and refuse new clients for up to an hour. This is the trade-off that item 1 of the request chose, and it is reachable only from inside the trusted local network. The self-hosting kit (e6a5cd22) could say so, or a later slice could bound local keys per /64 as well. I do not ask for a change in this head.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThere is one parser and one owner. The move removes 46 lines from limits.ts and adds 47 to Bytes, and the MCP change is 3 lines. The Page bundle change is generated output only. The tests replace the old one-line addressKey assertion in limits.test.ts with a focused Bytes file, and change existing Native witnesses instead of adding new ones. I see nothing to cut.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n  - The transport boundary is unchanged.\n  - Aliases and zones converge.\n  - Invalid addresses cannot bypass the limit.\n  - The raw bounds come before canonicalization.\n  - The local-key capacity effect is noted for the kit.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- Request conditions:\n  - addressKey and the bearer counter changed as stated, and the entry-points row is updated;\n  - the witnesses hold: separate link-local join windows, a shared global /64, link-local bearer failures counted apart, and V4.7 left as historical evidence;\n  - the original gate remains failed, and a separate full gate passed at the corrected source;\n  - order: after H1.\n\nThis approval covers the software head only. The Mac proxy validation was not repeated, and no LAN deployment is covered. The landing check will follow the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9e401d1c4369febc9c21cb34798f9c8a6aceb175","binding":"assigned","head":"cd9497ab433f41f86cfd164915af41299cd0ec35","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d4c5b1b88005dda16a59c55674e936acf1bb748a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a2d7366f1140c8fb86178f5cc77e1344f68ec87f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d4c5b1b88005dda16a59c55674e936acf1bb748a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}